---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Smarter ≠ Better — Luxon Learn" description="The expensive model isn't always the right choice. Sometimes fast beats pro.">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/legacy-shared.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/learn/learn-styles.css" />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Lesson Hero -->
  <section class="lesson-hero">
    <div class="lesson-breadcrumb">
      <a href="/learn">Learn</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>Lesson 7</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lesson-badge">Level 2</div>
    <h1>Smarter ≠ Better</h1>
    <p class="lesson-subtitle">The expensive model isn't always the right choice. Sometimes "fast" beats "pro."</p>
  </section>

  <div class="lesson-content">

    <!-- Visual: Pro model vs Fast model -->
    <div class="lesson-visual">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 300" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <!-- Pro model (expensive, overkill) -->
        <rect x="20" y="20" width="280" height="260" rx="16" fill="#fef2f2" stroke="#fecaca"/>
        <text x="160" y="52" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#dc2626" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">👑 PRO MODEL ($20/mo)</text>
        <!-- Speed gauge -->
        <rect x="50" y="72" width="220" height="20" rx="10" fill="#fee2e2"/>
        <rect x="50" y="72" width="55" height="20" rx="10" fill="#f87171"/>
        <text x="160" y="86" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">SLOW</text>
        <!-- Quality gauge -->
        <rect x="50" y="100" width="220" height="20" rx="10" fill="#fee2e2"/>
        <rect x="50" y="100" width="209" height="20" rx="10" fill="#f87171"/>
        <text x="160" y="114" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">95%</text>
        <!-- Cost -->
        <text x="50" y="148" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#dc2626">💰 $20/month</text>
        <text x="50" y="168" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#9ca3af">⏱️ 15 seconds per reply</text>
        <!-- Task -->
        <rect x="50" y="186" width="220" height="36" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#fecaca"/>
        <text x="160" y="200" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Task: "Summarize this email"</text>
        <text x="160" y="214" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">Overkill. Same result as fast model.</text>
        <!-- Bottom label -->
        <text x="50" y="258" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#dc2626" font-weight="600">❌ Paying for brainpower you don't need</text>

        <!-- Fast model (cheap, efficient) -->
        <rect x="340" y="20" width="280" height="260" rx="16" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#bbf7d0"/>
        <text x="480" y="52" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#16a34a" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">⚡ FAST MODEL ($5/mo)</text>
        <!-- Speed gauge -->
        <rect x="370" y="72" width="220" height="20" rx="10" fill="#dcfce7"/>
        <rect x="370" y="72" width="198" height="20" rx="10" fill="#4ade80"/>
        <text x="480" y="86" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">FAST</text>
        <!-- Quality gauge -->
        <rect x="370" y="100" width="220" height="20" rx="10" fill="#dcfce7"/>
        <rect x="370" y="100" width="176" height="20" rx="10" fill="#4ade80"/>
        <text x="480" y="114" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">80%</text>
        <!-- Cost -->
        <text x="370" y="148" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#16a34a">💰 $5/month</text>
        <text x="370" y="168" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#16a34a">⏱️ 3 seconds per reply</text>
        <!-- Task -->
        <rect x="370" y="186" width="220" height="36" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#86efac"/>
        <text x="480" y="200" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Task: "Summarize this email"</text>
        <text x="480" y="214" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="#16a34a" text-anchor="middle">Same result. 5x faster. 4x cheaper.</text>
        <!-- Bottom label -->
        <text x="370" y="258" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#16a34a" font-weight="600">✓ Right tool for the right job</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="lesson-visual-caption">For simple tasks, the fast model matches the pro model — at ¼ the cost and 5× the speed. Save the big gun for hard problems.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Steps -->
    <div class="lesson-steps">
      <div class="lesson-step">
        <div class="lesson-step__number">1</div>
        <div class="lesson-step__content">
          <h3>The 80/20 rule</h3>
          <p>80% of your daily AI tasks are simple: summaries, quick drafts, reformatting, translations. The fast model handles these perfectly. Save the expensive model for the 20% that need deep reasoning — complex analysis, creative writing, or multi-step logic.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lesson-step">
        <div class="lesson-step__number">2</div>
        <div class="lesson-step__content">
          <h3>Match model to task</h3>
          <p>Quick question? Fast model. Long document analysis? Pro model. Simple rewrite? Fast. Creative brainstorming? Pro. The key question: "Would a smart intern get this right?" If yes — use the fast model.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lesson-step">
        <div class="lesson-step__number">3</div>
        <div class="lesson-step__content">
          <h3>Start fast, escalate if needed</h3>
          <p>Default to the fast model. If the answer isn't good enough, paste the conversation into the pro model and say "improve this." You'll save time and money — most tasks never need the upgrade.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Tip -->
    <div class="lesson-tip">
      <div class="lesson-tip__icon">💡</div>
      <div class="lesson-tip__text"><strong>Pro tip:</strong> ChatGPT lets you switch models mid-conversation. Claude has Haiku (fast) and Sonnet/Opus (pro). Use the cheap one by default — upgrade only when you hit the ceiling.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="lesson-cta">
      <h3>Want this set up for you?</h3>
      <p>We configure everything — personalization, projects, and workflows — in one session.</p>
      <a href="https://wa.me/85297381028" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book installation</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Lesson Nav -->
  <div class="lesson-nav">
    <a href="/learn/lesson-6" class="prev"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="16" height="16"><path d="M19 12H5m7-7-7 7 7 7"/></svg> Let AI Write Its Own Instructions</a>
    <a href="/learn/lesson-8" class="next">Search Your Past Chats <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="16" height="16"><path d="M5 12h14m-7-7 7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
